1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,359
Pasting the same long review

2
00:00:01,379 --> 00:00:03,850
standards every time you ask Claude to review a PR?

3
00:00:03,870 --> 00:00:06,187
Skills fix that: write the process down once

4
00:00:06,207 --> 00:00:08,321
and Claude pulls it in when needed.

5
00:00:08,341 --> 00:00:11,233
A skill is a folder with a SKILL.md: a name

6
00:00:11,253 --> 00:00:13,561
and description first, then the actual steps.

7
00:00:13,581 --> 00:00:15,961
Keep it in your personal folder to use it everywhere,

8
00:00:15,981 --> 00:00:18,441
or in the project to share it with the team.

9
00:00:18,461 --> 00:00:19,933
The key difference:

10
00:00:19,953 --> 00:00:21,771
it isn't loaded into context all at once.

11
00:00:21,791 --> 00:00:24,392
Claude first sees only each skill's name and description,

12
00:00:24,412 --> 00:00:26,741
and loads the full contents once one matches.

13
00:00:26,761 --> 00:00:29,083
CLAUDE.md is the rulebook loaded every session;

14
00:00:29,103 --> 00:00:32,121
a skill is a manual opened only when needed.

15
00:00:32,141 --> 00:00:34,768
Type a slash and the skill name to call it, or let

16
00:00:34,788 --> 00:00:38,211
Claude decide. Edits take effect right away, no restart.

17
00:00:38,231 --> 00:00:39,693
The course's rule of thumb:

18
00:00:39,713 --> 00:00:41,668
type the same multi-step instruction twice,

19
00:00:41,688 --> 00:00:43,001
and it's a skill.

20
00:00:43,021 --> 00:00:44,401
Like the ones in the video:

21
00:00:44,421 --> 00:00:47,141
commit messages, PR descriptions, debugging, documentation.

22
00:00:47,161 --> 00:00:49,233
For workflows with side effects, like deploys,

23
00:00:49,253 --> 00:00:51,081
make the skill manual-only.

24
00:00:51,101 --> 00:00:53,153
Don't celebrate yet: every skill's description sits

25
00:00:53,173 --> 00:00:55,701
in context on every turn, so skip the ones you won't use.

26
00:00:55,721 --> 00:00:57,710
Always-on rules go in CLAUDE.md.

27
00:00:57,730 --> 00:01:00,091
Occasional manuals become skills.
